.. attr:: section[heat]
   :type: dict

   The attributes available for configuring a Heat section. Sections define
   the connection and detailed configuration that providers reference.

   .. attr:: connection
      :type: str
      :required:

      The name of the :ref:`connection <connections>` to use.

   .. attr:: region
      :type: str

      Default OpenStack region for this section. Can be overridden at the
      label level.

   .. attr:: resource-limits
      :type: dict

      Global resource limits across all stacks for this provider.

      .. attr:: stacks
         :type: int

         The maximum number of active Heat stacks across all labels
         for this provider.

      .. attr:: instances
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Nova instances across all stacks.

      .. attr:: cores
         :type: int

         Maximum total CPU cores across all stacks.

      .. attr:: ram
         :type: int

         Maximum total RAM in MiB across all stacks.

      .. attr:: volumes
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Cinder volumes across all stacks.

      .. attr:: volume-gb
         :type: int

         Maximum total volume storage in GB across all stacks.

      .. attr:: networks
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Neutron networks across all stacks.

      .. attr:: routers
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Neutron routers across all stacks.

      .. attr:: routers-with-external-gw
         :type: int

         Maximum number of routers with external gateway interfaces
         across all stacks.

      .. attr:: floating-ips
         :type: int

         Maximum number of floating IPs across all stacks.

   .. attr:: template-policy
      :type: dict

      Policy for controlling which Heat template features are permitted.
      This includes allowed resource types and intrinsic functions.
      Patterns are treated as Python regular expressions matched against
      the full resource type or function name (using fullmatch semantics).

      .. attr:: allowed-resource-types
         :type: list

         List of allowed Heat resource types. If specified, templates
         may only use resource types that match at least one pattern.
         Each entry is a Python regular expression:

         - Exact match: ``OS::Nova::Server``
         - Prefix match: ``^OS::Nova::.*`` (all Nova resources)
         - Complex: ``^OS::(Nova::(?!KeyPair$)|Neutron::(?!RBACPolicy$)|Cinder)::.*``
         - Negative lookahead: ``^(?!OS::Keystone::).*``
           (allow everything except Keystone resources)

      .. attr:: allowed-intrinsic-functions
         :type: list

         List of allowed HOT intrinsic functions. If specified, templates
         may only use intrinsic functions that match at least one pattern.
         Each entry is a Python regular expression matched against the
         function name.

   .. attr:: labels
      :type: list

      .. attr:: region
         :type: str

         OpenStack region where Heat stacks should be created. If omitted,
         uses the default region from the cloud configuration.

      .. attr:: flavor
         :type: str

         Flavor name for this label.

      .. attr:: image
         :type: str

         Image name for this label.

      .. attr:: external-network
         :type: str

         The name or ID of the external network for floating IPs.
         Passed to the Heat template as the ``zuul_external_network``
         parameter.  If omitted, the driver auto-discovers the first
         external IPv4 network from Neutron.

      .. attr:: key-name
         :type: str

         The name of a keypair that will be used when booting the node.

      .. attr:: host-key-checking
         :type: bool
         :default: true

         Whether to validate SSH host keys. When true, this helps ensure
         that nodes are ready to receive SSH connections before they are
         used.

   .. attr:: flavors
      :type: list

      .. note::

         In the Heat driver, flavors define **per-stack resource budgets**
         (upper limits on what a single stack may consume), not Nova flavor
         names.  The actual resource cost is determined by parsing the Heat
         template at request time.

      .. attr:: name
         :type: str
         :required:

         Flavor name.

      .. attr:: max-instances
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Nova instances allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-cores
         :type: int

         Maximum total CPU cores allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-ram
         :type: int

         Maximum total RAM in MiB allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-volumes
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Cinder volumes allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-volume-gb
         :type: int

         Maximum total volume storage in GB allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-networks
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Neutron networks allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-routers
         :type: int

         Maximum number of Neutron routers allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-routers-with-external-gw
         :type: int

         Maximum number of routers with external gateway interfaces
         allowed per stack.

      .. attr:: max-floating-ips
         :type: int

         Maximum number of floating IPs allowed per stack.

   .. attr:: images
      :type: list

      .. attr:: name
         :type: str
         :required:

         Image name used in label configuration.

      .. attr:: type
         :type: str
         :required:

         The type of image. Must be ``cloud`` (an image that already
         exists in the provider).

      .. attr:: image-id
         :type: str

         The Glance image ID or name for the bastion node.  This is
         passed to the Heat template as the ``zuul_image`` parameter.

.. attr:: provider[heat]
   :type: dict

   The attributes available for configuring a Heat provider. Providers
   reference a section and specify which labels to expose.

   .. attr:: section
      :type: str
      :required:

      The name of the section to inherit configuration from.

   .. attr:: stack-create-timeout
      :type: int
      :default: 600

      Maximum time in seconds to wait for a Heat stack to reach
      CREATE_COMPLETE status. If stack creation exceeds this timeout,
      the node request will fail.

      Default: 600 (10 minutes)

   .. attr:: resource-limits
      :type: dict

      Provider-specific resource limits that override or supplement the
      section's limits. See :attr:`section[heat].resource-limits` for
      available attributes.

   .. attr:: template-policy
      :type: dict

      Provider-specific template policy. See
      :attr:`section[heat].template-policy` for available attributes.

   .. attr:: labels
      :type: list

      List of label names to expose through this provider. Labels must be
      defined in the referenced section.
